      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Discuss recurring faults, root causes, and corrective actions.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 33287,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, I've completed the root cause analysis for the top 3 recurring faults as part of T6. The full report is in A4. Here's the summary:\n1. Sealing Bar Failure: Caused by incorrect pressure settings, leading to premature wear.\n2. Film Tracking Errors: Misaligned sensor bracket, gets knocked out of place easily.\n3. Product Jams at Infeed: Worn conveyor guides creating a bottleneck.",
            "mentions": [
              11000,
              95118,
              386277,
              533175
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 386277,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "Thanks for the detailed analysis, @33287. The evidence in the report is clear. The sensor bracket issue has been a pain for a while.",
            "mentions": [
              33287
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 95118,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "We see that film tracking error a lot on night shift. We always thought it was just bad rolls of film.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M57",
            "speaker_id": 11000,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "For the sealing bar, can't we just replace it more often?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M58",
            "speaker_id": 33287,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "That's a temporary fix, not a solution. The root cause is the incorrect pressure. If we fix that, the bars will last as long as they're supposed to, saving us time and money.",
            "mentions": [
              11000
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M59",
